<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:53:52Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Putin and Xi in India for BRICS summit as Ukraine, Middle East wars loom</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:eba1859c09ae4389bc43bd2091d5e18c2872087c01494baee3cc734854ea66ae</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:52:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T02:08:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260911-putin-xi-india-brics-summit-ukraine-middle-east-wars--f89644d9206b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260911-putin-xi-india-brics-summit-ukraine-middle-east-wars" /><summary type="html">Russian President Vladimir Putin arrived in New Delhi on Friday for a two-day BRICS summit expected to focus on wars in Ukraine and the Middle East and economic challenges. Putin and Iran’s Masoud Pezeshkian are due to meet Prime Minister Narendra Modi, while China’s Xi Jinping is also expected to hold talks.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Trump absent as New York marks 25 years since 9/11 with first Muslim mayor</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:93122fe9bd864640b7d7b0c6f0d8a7aeb1b68ccfbc679aaa406dfdcb57216119</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:52:52Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T01:47:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260911-trump-new-york-25-years-9-11-muslim-mayor--1ab77d9771b3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260911-trump-new-york-25-years-9-11-muslim-mayor" /><summary type="html">New York marks the 25th anniversary of the Sept. 11 attacks on Friday, with President Donald Trump attending a ceremony at the Pentagon while Vice President JD Vance and four former presidents join commemorations at Ground Zero, where victims’ relatives will read the names of those killed.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Yemen's Iran-backed Houthi rebels seize strategic Red Sea port city of Mocha</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d03cc7ef5a76cdfb78a5e37b4a8c6bcc2c7c74215044e677571a83ff8c506c0d</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:52:55Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T22:55:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260910-yemen-houthis-city-red-sea-iran--0d8343d16cb2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260910-yemen-houthis-city-red-sea-iran" /><summary type="html">Yemen’s Houthis seized the strategic Red Sea port city of Mocha on Thursday as their offensive against Saudi-backed government forces intensified. Saudi Arabia launched dozens of airstrikes over the past 24 hours, the Houthis said, after the Iran-backed group carried out attacks on Saudi territory that wounded dozens of people.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Manchester United thrash Sabah in Champions League return as Fabregas's Como shine on European debut</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:27f2811b82c352a176478f5d6ca74d951b1131958c34a06359dd1119ceeeac73</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:52:58Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T22:25:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/sport/20260910-manchester-united-sabah-champions-league-fabregas-como-european-debut--e340158a2475.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/sport/20260910-manchester-united-sabah-champions-league-fabregas-como-european-debut" /><summary type="html">Manchester United marked their Champions League return with a 4-0 rout of Sabah on Thursday, with Matheus Cunha, Bruno Fernandes, Benjamin Sesko and Lisandro Martinez scoring. Bayern Munich thrashed Bodo/Glimt 5-0 as Ballon d'Or nominees Michael Olise struck twice and Harry Kane scored, while Cesc Fabregas's Como impressed on their competition debut.</summary><category term="Sport" /></entry><entry><title>Israel destroys Hezbollah tunnel network in south Lebanon, triggering 4.1-magnitude tremor</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:312b95b8f0153530f9148bc64f9f12c0f8144b54a60af2d3fec275809e38aee5</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:53:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T21:50:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260910-israel-hezbollah-tunnels-lebanon-earthquake--c28ae45e8d7b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260910-israel-hezbollah-tunnels-lebanon-earthquake" /><summary type="html">Israel said on Thursday it destroyed key tunnels built by Iran-backed Hezbollah beneath the strategic Ali al-Taher ridge in southern Lebanon, completing what it called operational control of the area. Lebanon reported a massive explosion, while the US Geological Survey recorded a magnitude 4.1 tremor nearby.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Space: Europe urged to find its path, from crewed spaceflight to communications</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0f3f7ddf98ed1b8fc33d5c332c957fa7a006c6a1ac952603046b1d9f420da5e6</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:53:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T21:05:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260910-space-europe-urged-to-find-its-path-from-crewed-spaceflight-to-communications--2c4f857a80db.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260910-space-europe-urged-to-find-its-path-from-crewed-spaceflight-to-communications" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron and European Commission President Ursula von der Leyen called on Thursday for Europeans to "act" on a massive scale to find their place against the United States and China in the space race, from communications to crewed spaceflight. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney, Svetla Ben-Itzhak, Assistant Professor of Space and International Relations, and Deputy Director of the West Space Scholars Programme at Johns Hopkins University, explains that "Europe does have world-class scientific and industrial capabilities, as well as aspirations, but it lacks the investment, the launch cadence, the scale as well as the degree of political integration that the US and China possess".</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry><entry><title>Ugandan royal succession scandal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:28ecdaef91ca57a05eb32243f96f437357e4e9259147b3b220f1489670b2bbcc</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:53:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T20:20:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ugandan-royal-succession-scandal--dc969309a6f8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ugandan-royal-succession-scandal" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition, a dramatic struggle for control of a throne in Uganda. Also, Rwanda shut down 101 alcoholic beverage factories last month and declared a public health crisis after at least 50 people were killed by contaminated illegal supplies. And Ethiopia celebrates its new year.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>🔴 Live: Israel demolition of Hezbollah tunnels in south Lebanon caused 4.1-magnitude quake</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8cce1efaaf3772abcbf9ecf447f7c8d42db8b4efd81b11a977ae334faab359ea</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:53:10Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T20:12:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260910-middle-east-live-trump-warns-iran-not-to-get-cute-over-activity-at-pickaxe-mountain--16e2d74b863a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260910-middle-east-live-trump-warns-iran-not-to-get-cute-over-activity-at-pickaxe-mountain" /></entry><entry><title>Record heat and drought make this year's champagne stronger</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:49decd3a04be348250a3e35f5f429ce17cb4ff4affd13552d5f465fb0e499c62</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:53:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T20:12:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20260910-record-heat-and-drought-make-this-year-s-champagne-stronger--3cf2d8750a3d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20260910-record-heat-and-drought-make-this-year-s-champagne-stronger" /><summary type="html">For the first time, French champagne producers are allowed to sell their bubbly with more than 13% alcohol, as record heatwaves and drought have resulted in grapes containing unusually high levels of sugar. They fear that climate change may eventually force them to permanently rewrite the rules governing winemaking.  Also in the segment, the European Central Bank raised interest rates for the second time this year amid higher energy costs, as a potential new gas crisis looms over Europe.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Meta tests out putting fact-checking in users’ hands across Latin America</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:110e57ad913d2b9c4943d1042a9b38672c3f4b4a124cd1884115607e0a100624</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:53:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T20:11:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/meta-tests-out-putting-fact-checking-in-users-hands-across-latin-america-1--ff193be16a97.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/meta-tests-out-putting-fact-checking-in-users-hands-across-latin-america-1" /><summary type="html">Meta is expanding its shift away from professional fact-checking. The tech giant announced it's trialling it's crowdsourced "Community Notes" system across 16 countries in Latin America. Meta says the system will only fully roll out once it is confident it works, but critics warn that with misinformation, manipulated images and AI-generated content spreading rapidly, crowdsourced checks may come too late to prevent false claims from reaching millions. Vedika Bahl explains the risks.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>French firefighters on six-week strike after record summer blazes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dfbda5b99e0d4d652db96b67e14a25c26e0919330ae1f2fe34e32bf134156b1c</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:53:19Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T19:41:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/french-firefighters-on-six-week-strike-after-record-summer-blazes--21f0641fbc58.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/french-firefighters-on-six-week-strike-after-record-summer-blazes" /><summary type="html">Firefighters in France are on strike over a lack of funding for essential emergency services. Their dedication was pushed to the limit in the recent wild fire episodes south of Paris and near Bordeaux. Short comings in the current system were highlighted by these extreme cases. FRANCE 24's Mark Owen speaks with Yael Lecras, Vice-President of the National Union of Professional Firefighters.</summary></entry><entry><title>As New York marks 25 years since 9/11, Muslims recall stigmatisation in aftermath of attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:496679d140ac715ddfb3eff1f98c2f0ddd0e9171b72264bb1dea5468c73caebf</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:53:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T19:32:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/as-new-york-marks-25-years-since-9-11-muslims-recall-stigmatization-in-aftermath-of-attacks--138f5fff2da5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/as-new-york-marks-25-years-since-9-11-muslims-recall-stigmatization-in-aftermath-of-attacks" /><summary type="html">As New York marks 25 years since the terrorist attacks on September 11th, New York’s Muslim community has become increasingly part of the fabric of the city. One sign of that is the election of Zohran Mamdani as the city’s mayor last November. Another is the state's largest mosque, due to open its doors at the end of the year. But while things have improved, many Muslims still remember the difficult months that followed the attack. FRANCE 24's Monte Francis reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>'No facts': Morocco denies involvement in deadly Ceuta migrant rush</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1beef649a2a0873b8845ca89de8f3e781765cea31dd3d72c1ceef2ca3b11adf6</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:53:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T19:32:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260910-no-facts-morocco-denies-involvement-in-deadly-ceuta-migrant-rush--ae85c7241bed.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260910-no-facts-morocco-denies-involvement-in-deadly-ceuta-migrant-rush" /><summary type="html">Moroccan authorities said on Thursday there were "no facts" establishing its involvement in the migrant rush into Spain's North African exclave of Ceuta in July. It was the kingdom's first official response to a Spanish police report accusing its security forces of "total permissiveness" when the mass crossing took place.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Iran-backed Houthi rebels take strategic port city in Yemen, raising threat to Red Sea shipping</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b7cae37672b8e1faa9569f9b0a399d699eca970dc1be18e5261bd08eba5d6ef3</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:53:28Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T19:18:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/iran-backed-houthi-rebels-take-strategic-port-city-in-yemen-raising-threat-to-red-sea-shipping--ea40bb9d282d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/iran-backed-houthi-rebels-take-strategic-port-city-in-yemen-raising-threat-to-red-sea-shipping" /><summary type="html">The Iran-backed Houthi rebel group on Thursday took over Yemen’s port city of Mokha, an area vital to controlling shipping through the Red Sea, Houthi and Yemeni officials said. Mokha is about 80 kilometers (50 miles) from the Bab el-Mandeb Strait, a waterway that connects the Red Sea and the Gulf of Aden and through which about 12% of the world’s goods are typically shipped. FRANCE 24's Nick Rushworth reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Iran raises fuel prices for heavy users</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:84628477ed23dbe019b2ffff71a9e8a44ad3bd6a859e88e7ccdbf5d227836b39</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:53:32Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T18:48:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/iran-raises-fuel-prices-for-heavy-users--e0de25d0e71c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/iran-raises-fuel-prices-for-heavy-users" /><summary type="html">The rise of the price of fuel is an issue for both the United States and Iran in this conflict. US president Donald Trump has conceded that prices will not fall before the midterm elections where the US voters could hold him to account. Meanwhile in Iran where many communities have been bombed since February 28th, there's now the added problem of incresing fuel prices. FRANCE 24's Ali al Basha sent this report.</summary></entry><entry><title>9/11 then and now: Do September 2001 attacks still shape our world?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:57054d6e15349120d203ccc60e3a421d6adc6f4383d162c9d269c445921ae2ff</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:53:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T18:17:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260910-9-11-then-and-now-do-september-2001-attacks-still-shape-our-world--b22b4497a9ae.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260910-9-11-then-and-now-do-september-2001-attacks-still-shape-our-world" /><summary type="html">Once in a generation, sometimes once in a lifetime, a singular event blindsides the entire planet. 25 years on, does the memory of the Nine-Eleven attacks against New York's Twin Towers, the Pentagon and in Pennsylvania fade into history or is it still as raw and vivid as on that sunny September morning?</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>French govt warns right-wing TV channel about rebroadcasting expelled pro-Putin pundit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e689104c3c5118f69f9217b33e2f07205188929d96858f84395b38116051a42a</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:53:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T17:52:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20260910-french-govt-warns-right-wing-tv-channel-about-using-expelled-pro-putin-pundit--d3fc6b965aed.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260910-french-govt-warns-right-wing-tv-channel-about-using-expelled-pro-putin-pundit" /><summary type="html">France's government on Thursday condemned the return of expelled Russian commentator Xenia Federova to conservative TV channel, CNews, for alleged Kremlin ties. Federova was formally expelled from France in August over claims she was a Kremlin agent and accusations that she spread Kremlin propaganda on French television and radio.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>What to know about Trump's pledge of $5,000 to 'every American' if GOP wins midterms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:edf6a13358a615aabd1e73f4dd452f6944da7c666d0e218cf4fe5f13ee5640cc</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:53:40Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T17:39:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260910-what-to-know-about-trump-s-5-000-dividend-pledge--bf5bef619ba0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260910-what-to-know-about-trump-s-5-000-dividend-pledge" /><summary type="html">President Donald Trump ⁠promised a $5,000 "Trump dividend" ​payment to every US adult on Wednesday if his Republicans retain control of the House of Representatives and the Senate in the November 3 midterm elections. The pledge has raised numerous questions. Here's what we know so far.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Céline Dion: Fan recounts experience singing with the superstar</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a15bf3e5fe8e479e2e29710497725bd10246d9a4f13e16e9aaa0860d0eda3880</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:53:43Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T16:08:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260910-c_line-dion-fan-recounts-experience-singing-with-the-superstar--9029daa90d55.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260910-c%C3%A9line-dion-fan-recounts-experience-singing-with-the-superstar" /><summary type="html">His childhood dream came true - and he went viral for it. Sacha Dally, 20, got the chance to sing a duet with Céline Dion when he met the Canadian superstar outside her Paris hotel, impressing her with his vocals. He tells FRANCE 24 about his experience.</summary></entry><entry><title>Hindu sect BAPS comes under scrutiny in France, US</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6d90b3247fe76186dbb4280dd5dc5a34bfa248e7328c659ea76855d2ac41f13a</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:53:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T16:06:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/hindu-sect-baps-comes-under-scrutiny-in-france-us--f1ba839b328f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/hindu-sect-baps-comes-under-scrutiny-in-france-us" /><summary type="html">France got a crash course on BAPS, the Hindu sect at the heart of an Eiffel Tower strike this week. But for Indians in France who have been trying to raise awareness of far-right Hindu groups, it comes too late. The sect came under scrutiny in the US more than five years ago. Now French public opinion is asking how the group got the green light for a mega temple near Paris and why questions were not raised.</summary></entry><entry><title>🔴 Middle East live: Houthis close in on Bab el-Mandeb as Brent barrel price soars to over $106</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e8ea6873a5df2c4b11e64941db5e08303f96eef150e97392ef65bee4cf8cbe29</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:53:10Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T16:06:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260910-middle-east-live-trump-warns-iran-not-to-get-cute-over-activity-at-pickaxe-mountain--16e2d74b863a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260910-middle-east-live-trump-warns-iran-not-to-get-cute-over-activity-at-pickaxe-mountain" /></entry><entry><title>August hottest month ever recorded globally as huge El Nino emerges</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:209e7ac093b3eda3ab52e52f137233b8e50d8443e932451a7a4383bb9a23abb7</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:53:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T15:57:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260910-august-hottest-month-ever-recorded-globally-as-huge-el-nino-emerges--0f748e2e0e26.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260910-august-hottest-month-ever-recorded-globally-as-huge-el-nino-emerges" /><summary type="html">Europe's climate monitor said Thursday that August was the hottest month ever recorded around the world and warned of worse to come, as an unprecedented El Nino pattern grows stronger. Global temperatures over land and sea soared to all-time highs in August and capped an extreme summer of heatwaves and wildfires that ranked the hottest on record for western Europe and the contiguous United States.</summary></entry><entry><title>Zelensky's plane 'almost hit' by drone en route to Oslo, Norway PM says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:857676261df75297b80e4d1bf3b5db1d3fa292b77d6a733ac39cf28c5f7f1ee4</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:53:52Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T15:55:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260910-zelensky-s-plane-almost-hit-by-drone-en-route-to-oslo-norway-pm-says--d5e48beb9256.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260910-zelensky-s-plane-almost-hit-by-drone-en-route-to-oslo-norway-pm-says" /><summary type="html">Ukraine and Moldova on Wednesday played down claims from Norway's prime minister that a plane carrying President Volodymyr Zelensky was almost hit by a drone as it flew to Oslo. Jonas Gahr Store told Norwegian public broadcaster NRK that Zelensky's plane was "almost hit by a drone when it was taking off from Moldova". But a source in the Ukrainian presidency described the claim that Zelensky was at risk as "exaggerated".</summary></entry></feed>
